# Auto push and deploy

When a task is done and there are real code changes the user would want live:

1. Commit with a short message that explains why (HEREDOC, no `--no-verify`).
2. `git push origin HEAD` to `main` (this GitHub remote). Never force-push.
3. Vercel deploys from `main` automatically — no extra CLI unless push failed.
4. Tell the user the live URL: https://myportfolio-web-xi.vercel.app

Do this without waiting to be asked again. Skip only if there is nothing to commit, the user said not to ship, or the change is local-only (rules, notes).
